                                                <description>I ordered this monitor on Amazon about a week ago for $749, but the shipping was set for the first week of September. When I saw this deal come up, I canceled the Amazon order right away and picked...</description>
                                                <content:encoded><![CDATA[<div><img src="https://static.slickdealscdn.com/attachment/2/5/4/6/2/4/300x300/18157717.thumb" alt="MSI 49&quot; Curved OLED Display, 144Hz 0.03ms, Gaming Monitor - $679.00" height="300" width="300"></div><br /><div>Thumb Score: +41 </div><div>I ordered this monitor on Amazon about a week ago for $749, but the shipping was set for the first week of September. When I saw this deal come up, I canceled the Amazon order right away and picked it up from Sam's Club instead.<br />
<br />
The 144Hz refresh rate should work well for what I do. I don't play esports games, and you'd probably need something like an RTX 4090 to really get the most out of 240Hz anyway. It comes with a built-in KVM switch and no bloated Samsung software pre-installed. <br />
<br />
I think it has the latest panel, and a recent firmware update has made the OLED protection features a bit less noticeable. This seems like a really good price. I'm looking forward to trying out games like Cyberpunk 2077 or Red Dead Redemption 2 on it.</div>
]]></content:encoded>
